<br/>
<br/>Note that Tier is not available until the Heart of Fear raid is released, and the Celestial version of Tier is not available until two weeks after Heart of Fear has been released. For that reason you will generally just be looking at non Tier items with a high Item Level until these items are available to you. Make sure you are always simming your gear when either introducing set bonuses or breaking them, as your other gear can heavily impact whether or not using new items is worth it.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Unholy Death Knight Trinkets in Phase 1</span></h2>As an Unholy Death Knight you generally want trinkets that yield the highest amount of Strength as possible, as this is your most precious Stat due to multiple modifiers.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Unholy Death Knights typically want two passive trinkets as they can be used in conjunction with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a>, granting the highest amount of Strength as possible. Since every single damage dealing ability of a Death Knight scales with Strength, it is also your most desireable stat by far. <br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89083/iron-belly-wok">
<img alt="Iron Belly Wok" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_cooking_masterofthewok.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Iron Belly Wok</span></a> is not the greatest trinket but is still a powerful early option and has the added bonus of only costing Valor Points. It has a high amount of passive Strength which is nice. The fact that its active effect is Haste also makes it less punishing to use as an Engineer.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81268/lessons-of-the-darkmaster">
<img alt="Lessons of the Darkmaster" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lessons of the Darkmaster</span></a> has a powerful on-use effect with a large amount of Strength. The added passive Expertise is nice for early gearing but the trinket itself is mostly undesirable when you reach the raiding stage.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is generally the best passive trinket until you have obtained your Heroic Raid BiS. It has passive Strength and a large proc that also grants Strength. While it is likely to be very expensive early on, this trinket is so incredibly powerful that you should make it your highest priority to obtain.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87072/lei-shens-final-orders">
<img alt="Lei Shen's Final Orders" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lei Shen's Final Orders</span></a> makes up one of our Phase 1 BiS trinkets. While it comes from the final boss of Mogu'shan Vaults, it is fortunately not too difficult to obtain as this raid is quite a bit easier than the others.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87172/darkmist-vortex">
<img alt="Darkmist Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_cyclone_nodebris.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmist Vortex</span></a> is our other BiS trinket. It drops of the arguably easiest boss in the raid, but is likely very contested by other Strength-classes. Assuming you already have your <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> it is also not the largest available upgrade from pre-raid BiS.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reputation for Unholy Death Knights in Phase 1</span></h2>Reputation gear can be very strong - especially in earlier stages of gearing. These items are mostly relevant during the Mogu'shan Vaults phase where you especially want <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89345/stonetoe-spaulders">
