<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Unholy Death Knights</span></h2>Almost every profession is viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic, but some are a bit more powerful than others - particularly for classes that want Secondary Stats like Crit and Haste. This is the case for Unholy Death Knights in particular.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Unholy Death Knights</h4>Blacksmithing brings with it the now traditional additional Sockets with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55628/socket-bracer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_socketedbracer.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Bracer</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55641/socket-gloves">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_addsocketglove.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Gloves</span></a>, giving a flexible stat choice that can be very strong. This offers adding additional Strength and Crit or Haste to your Stat pool, which makes Blacksmithing the best choice for professions when it comes to raiding.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="jewelcrafting">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_jewelcrafting.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Jewelcrafting for Unholy Death Knights</h4>Jewelcrafting is often seen as one of the strongest professions, and looking at the various <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76734/serpents-eye">
<img alt="Serpent's Eye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_sc_eyeofacherus_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Serpent's Eye</span></a>, it's no surprise why. Jewelcrafters can equip 2 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=83141/bold-serpents-eye">
<img alt="Bold Serpent's Eye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Serpent's Eye</span></a> for a big jump in Strength. While Jewelcrafting is powerful, it does fall behind Blacksmithing due to these Jewelcrafting-specific gems only having single Stats.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Unholy Death Knights</h4>Engineering is as close to being mandatory as a profession can be. The power of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> cannot be understated, as it is essentially an extra trinket that can be used on top of your other procs. It also offers bombs and grenades which you can use to deal extra damage, as well as a myriad of gadgets.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Unholy Death Knights</span></h3>Crafted items are a great way of increasing your Item Level and power through gold. If you have a lot of gold to spend, this is where you sohould look out for items with great longevity and high item level, such as the items suggested below.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> has already been mentioned but deserves an extra mention. This Trinket is fantastic and should be a priority if you have the gold.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87402/ornate-battleplate-of-the-master">
<img alt="Ornate Battleplate of the Master" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raiddeathknight_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ornate Battleplate of the Master</span></a> is a great option for your Chest slot until you obtain items from raids. The Sockets, high Item Level and large amount of Expertise makes it a great stepping stone while gearing.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87407/bloodforged-warfists">
<img alt="Bloodforged Warfists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodforged Warfists</span></a> like the Chest has a large amount of Stats, particularly Hit, which makes it great to round off your Hit cap while gearing up.</div></li></ul>
